WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.767
-Since the last time you've been
here, I just want to tell you,

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.567
you were fantastic
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.868
-Thank you.
-You were a...

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
...unbelievable host.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.367
I loved every sketch,
everything you did.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.634
I go -- Man, you crushed it.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.400
That was a dream come true.
-Yeah.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.868
Were you nervous
at all doing it?

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:19.667
-I mean, I would say yes
except you're just too busy.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.267
You get rushed from one thing --
I mean, you know.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.601
I just didn't know.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.167
They're suddenly saying my name
and I'm walking out

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.367
and was like,
"Oh, this isn't rehearsal.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.467
We're actually -- This is live.
We're doing it."

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.634
-Live television.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:30.400
Yeah, they don't do live TV
anymore, yeah.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.200
But then they called you back.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.167
-I guess they were gonna do
a "Father of the Bride."

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.400
-You were in
"Father of the Bride."

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.467
Here you are.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.968
[ Audience awws ]

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.667
-Oh! He was once 9.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.033
-That's you.
-Yep.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.067
-And that's Steve Martin.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.000
-And then so they
did the sketch,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.200
a "Father of the Bride"
kind of reunion

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.734
with Martin Short and Steve.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.167
And here you are.
You showed up. It killed.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:56.801
In the same outfit.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.400
They did pretty well.
Yeah.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.767
-That's pretty good.

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.534
-That's what Matty Banks
would look like

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:02.734
about 30 years in the future.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.067
Yeah, that's right.
-Yeah.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.234
What was it like to reunite
with Marty and Steve?

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.701
-That was fantastic.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:08.834
I didn't think

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.100
they were actually gonna
go through with it

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.834
when they said, "Are you
available tomorrow to do --"

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.400
Tomorrow. It was like
getting the call like,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.734
"Would you show up to 'SNL'
and be Matty Banks?"

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:18.534
Yeah, sure. It'll happen.
-Yeah, why not, though, right?

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:19.534
-It was great.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.000
I always thought
there could be a sequel.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.167
There could be
"Father of the Bride 3"

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.467
or just one sketch on "SNL."

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.801
Beautifully done.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.133
-When you did
"Father of the Bride,"

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:28.534
"Home Alone" had just come out.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:29.968
And I'm assuming --

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.467
Were you and your brothers
always confused for each other?

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.501
-Often, yeah.
It still happens.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.968
I get confused for Rory a lot.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.801
The one that kind of
blew my mind,

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:42.467
when I was about that age, I got
out of a car at an airport,

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.567
and a woman ran up to me.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:44.734
She noticed me right away,

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.567
or thought she recognized me
right away,

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.834
and ran up and said,
"Are you Macluckly Macluckly?"

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.767
And I had the presence of mind
to go, "No, nobody is."

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.667
-Yeah, that's not
a human being's name.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.734
-That is not somebody's name.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.767
-It just isn't.
-But to this day,

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.834
do people go up
and they mistake you?

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.534
-Often, yeah, like, "You know,
I worked with you on 'Signs.'"

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.734
"Oh, yeah, was I a dick?
'Cause that was my brother."

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:07.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.000
-That's so funny.
-It was Rory.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.200
-That was Rory.
Yeah, of course.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.901
I want to talk
about "Succession"

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.868
because, man, you crush it
on this show.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.734
-Oh, thanks.
-This is the beginning...

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.634
...of the fourth
and final season.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.033
It starts on Sunday.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.367
Are you gonna miss
playing Roman?

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:28.934
-I think so.
It hasn't hit me,

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.501
'cause we only finished
like three weeks ago shooting.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.300
I just have not processed it.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.567
I'm pretty sure, yeah --
what's the thing --

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:36.567
depression, that'll hit.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.100
-Yeah, that will come in soon.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.901
A lot of fans of yours
think that Roman

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:44.000
doesn't understand chairs
and how they work,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.801
because every time
you're sitting,

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:48.167
it's always the oddest position
I've ever seen.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.667
-Yeah.
That's one of the most --

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.234
-This is one.
Here's another one.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.234
-Yeah, yeah. Alright.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:59.367
-And then here's a third one
here of you on top of the --

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.167
-Nice face, by the way. Yeah.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.567
-You just don't normally sit
in a chair.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.100
-Yeah, there's a lot
of upside down.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.234
I didn't notice that until
after like the second season

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:08.667
people started
pointing that out.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.467
And a lot of people,
including my wife,

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.734
thought that that was, like,
something I was told --

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.901
It was either in the writing
or the director said,

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.067
"Can you go upside down
on a chair or something?"

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.901
-"Can you just like crouch
in the corner on a chair?"

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.534
-Yeah, I've been told
that it's weird.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.200
I didn't even notice
I was doing it,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.133
and then I tried to forget
that I heard that

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.000
'cause I don't want
to stop sitting weird.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.734
I've already established
that he does that now.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.434
I got to keep it up.
-Yeah, now you got to do it.

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:33.334
I guess, yeah.
Give the people what they want.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.701
Last time we talked,
you came on the show,

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.801
I think you were
supposed to audition

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.033
for Nicholas Braun's role,
cousin Greg,

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.067
but then I heard --
is this true --

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.834
that Jeremy Strong
was originally cast to be Roman?

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.400
-I think that's when he --
he had picked to be Roman.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.467
That's what I heard.

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.300
Like, he was given
the script first

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.033
and said he wanted
to play Roman.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.767
I was given it to read
for cousin Greg,

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.400
and I didn't feel
I was right for it,

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:01.067
so I just sent in a tape
without asking for Roman, so...

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:04.200
-So Jeremy goes, "I'm gonna --
I don't want to be Roman."

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.667
-I don't know. I know that
he wanted to be initially.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.400
But I can't, like, picture it.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.367
I can't picture being Greg
and him being Roman.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.601
What a very odd --
-Yeah.

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.968
But it would be odd Roman.
Yeah, you guys are perfect.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.968
The way it is right now
is the perfect cast.

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.634
-Yeah.
-And it's --

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.767
Dude, everybody is fantastic,
including you.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.434
-Oh, thanks.
-Yeah.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:27.934
-Including me, wow.
-Yeah, including you.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.400
We can add applause in post.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.300
We have 10 episodes left.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.434
What can we expect
for the final season?

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.467
Oh, my goodness.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:41.567
You can expect 10 episodes
of the fourth and final season.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.000
I don't know what else to say.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.200
-You really -- Yeah,
you can't spoil anything.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.334
-I can't and I wouldn't want to,
I feel like,

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:49.100
'cause I saw Brian
was on your show

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.901
I think yesterday
or the day before.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.501
-He was so funny, by the way.
-He's hilarious.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:54.701
Like, what the heck.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.267
And, yeah, he said he thinks

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.701
that each season got better
than the last,

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.334
and I would agree with that.

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:01.834
-He said kind of to me,
he goes --

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.434
I go, "Do you think it's gonna
be the final season?"

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:06.567
He goes, "I don't
really feel like --

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:08.067
I think we could've gone more."

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.234
'Cause it almost feels like
when a show gets popular,

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.467
now is when you get re-upped
for another three seasons

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:13.801
and you go --
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:15.934
I mean, it could've gone more.
And I feel like --

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.367
And the way that we end,

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:20.267
it feels sort of like
there still could be more,

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.667
but I think it's also
a satisfying end.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.033
It's nice.
I don't know.

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:27.968
It's like if the options were
go out a high

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.501
when there could be more or stay
at the party a little too long,

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:31.934
I'd rather take
the former, so...

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:34.400
-Yeah, yeah, so you left
the party at the right time.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.734
-I guess so.
Well, you never know.

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.868
If there was a five,
that could've been great.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.133
I'm saying, Jesse,
write a fifth season.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.434
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:44.100
It's so good.
It's so clever.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.000
It's so well-acted.
It's so funny.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:48.467
Here's Kieran Culkin
in "Succession."

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:49.968
Take a look.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:54.334
-So my question was, uh, would
you consider giving him a call?

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:58.434
-Would we consider
at least a call?

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:01.667
-Uh...was he apologizing?

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.968
-Did -- I mean, did he ask?

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:05.801
-Um, did he ask?

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:09.534
-Uh, he -- I just --

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:12.400
I know that he would love
to hear from you.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.234
-I mean, if he were to call,
then we would see.

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:18.234
-Yeah, I think it's just gonna
be a lot to get him to call,

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:19.634
just knowing him.

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:22.434
-Yeah, I mean, I think we know
him pretty well, actually.

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:25.300
I mean, we've never licked
his big omelet nipples, but --

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.267
-I could get him to text
a request for a call.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:30.534
-Text?

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:33.267
I'm afraid we're gonna need
to hear that voice.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.000
Okay, you can pop it back
in your mouth now.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.667
We're getting on the plane.
Thanks. Bye.

00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:39.734
-Come on.
Kieran Culkin, everybody.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:42.601
The fourth and final season
of "Succession"

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.467
premieres on HBO this Sunday.

